Dear Zoe and Brent,

=20

Thank you for your time yesterday and for your advice with regards to the O=
xus/Borealis merger and Newco=E2=80=99s debut on Nasdaq on 8 February 2024 under t=
he ticker symbol BRLS.

=20

With regards to Imerman, I am not satisfied with doing nothing because not =
only it is a hugely unfair and inequitable outcome, but also the devices con=
tain forensic evidence of criminal activities which represent a direct finan=
cial risk to me in the future and therefore should, at a minimum, be preserv=
ed in escrow. Please see the attached correspondence clip and the summary do=
cument titled =E2=80=9CImerman".
The respondent asked me to pause the Imerman process in order to save costs=
 and reach a settlement via mediation. In her letter to HFC dated 20 May 202=
1 (page 10), Diana Parker was extremely clear that the process would resume =
should we fail to reach a settlement. Since the FDR in July 2021 the respond=
ent has systematically opposed all my attempts to resume the Imerman process=
.=20
On 20th November 2023, Zoe wrote to the respondent=E2=80=99s solicitors in order =
to resume the Imerman process.
Their reply of 21 November 2023 is attached.=20
The Imerman review is my right and the respondent=E2=80=99s duty. The guidance in=
 UL v BK reads: =E2=80=9CThe husband's solicitor, who owes a high duty to the cour=
t, will read [the Imerman documents] and disclose those of them that are bot=
h admissible and relevant to the wife's claim, pursuant to the husband's dut=
y of full and frank disclosure=E2=80=9D.
Given the non-disclosures in this case, the importance of crypto assets, an=
d the respondent=E2=80=99s litigation conduct, it is extremely unfair that I am be=
ing denied my rights for an equitable and just process.=20
I was not able to undertake the Imerman process because the respondent used=
 his unlimited resources to oppose it, while he starved me of liquidity.
The respondent=E2=80=99s efforts to obstruct due process of justice should be con=
sidered and the harm he has caused me should not be compounded by the very i=
nstitution which is supposed to grant fairness and equity.
=20

Further considerations:
The respondent=E2=80=99s review of the hard copy Imerman documents was woefully d=
ishonest and misleading.
As with everything else in these proceedings, I only found out three years =
later when my brother explained to me what a node was.
Paul Sibenik=E2=80=99s review of the Imerman hard copy documents is attached.=20
Sibenik=E2=80=99s review demonstrates that the respondent=E2=80=99s narrative of 24 Jun=
e 2021 is completely false.=20
Sibenik=E2=80=99s review supports the claim that the respondent=E2=80=99s crypto activi=
ties are institutional.
=20

The other important consideration is that the MacBook Pro computer held in =
escrow contains forensic evidence of the respondent=E2=80=99s activities related t=
o money laundering of prostitution proceeds. I mentioned this in my conduct =
statement as well as my section 25. Given the ongoing criminal investigation=
 and the potential risk of asset forfeiture, the devices should not be retur=
ned to the respondent.

=20

Please consider the attached documents and let me know what my legal option=
s are.

=20

With kind wishes,

Nadia

=20

BV20D01752

Fraud Unravels All=20

Veritas Numquam Perit

UK: +44 79 1332 8615

US: +1 424 426 9226


